1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,218
Education does not need another answer box.

2
00:00:04,218 --> 00:00:09,640
Canopy turns nine subjects into visible, interactive reasoning journeys.

3
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:15,127
A six-stage constellation moves from observation to modeling and validation.

4
00:00:15,127 --> 00:00:21,423
The final stage transfers knowledge while one teacher preserves the learner's context.

5
00:00:21,663 --> 00:00:24,460
Switch to Romanian or Arabic.

6
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:32,850
Twenty languages translate the full learning surface, and right-to-left layout keeps scientific models correctly oriented.

7
00:00:33,090 --> 00:00:34,744
A learner explains.

8
00:00:34,744 --> 00:00:44,673
Canopy reveals evidence, confidence, a misconception hypothesis, mastery, and the next question instead of hiding behind a score.

9
00:00:44,913 --> 00:00:52,487
Its optional multilingual model can run inside the browser using Web G P U or Web Assembly.

10
00:00:52,487 --> 00:00:57,833
The inspectable local rubric remains available without an account or API key.

11
00:00:58,073 --> 00:01:01,419
Teachers paste their material into Course Forge.

12
00:01:01,419 --> 00:01:08,113
Canopy extracts six editable stages locally and requires teacher review before anything is saved.

13
00:01:08,353 --> 00:01:20,516
The evidence view reports only observed interactions: explanation quality, recovery time, and a course heatmap, never invented pilot results.

14
00:01:20,756 --> 00:01:28,386
The device-local learner model keeps mastery, misconceptions, spaced review, and portable exports.

15
00:01:28,386 --> 00:01:35,379
Voice, screen-reader announcements, contrast, dyslexia-friendly type, and reduced motion widen access.

16
00:01:35,619 --> 00:01:47,999
Canopy ends with transfer: one accountable AI teacher across school science and the humanities, ready now in an ordinary browser.
